# Compact audio transformer model registry for PedalKernel.
#
# These are behavioral scalar models for the realtime WDF/MNA transformer path,
# not full vendor SPICE subcircuits. Units:
#   LP/LM/LLP/LLS = H, RP/RS/RC = Ohm, CP/CW = F, K = coupling coefficient.
# Geometry/core fields are carried for Phase 2/4 nonlinear-core work:
#   N1/N2 = turns, AE = m^2, LE/GAP = m, MS/A/ALPHA/JA_K/C = Jiles-Atherton,
#   HC/BR/BS = datasheet hysteresis hints.

# Core data (MS + N1/AE/LE) calibrated so the DERIVED saturation knee
# (`JaCoreModel::from_small_signal`, which fixes `a` from LM so the linear
# tangent stays == LM) sits at the part's rated max level @20Hz, ABOVE
# line-level stimulus → LINEAR at line, JA when driven near rated. The knee is
# never hand-set; geometry + material (from MS) place it. See the per-model
# notes for the rated level and its [DATASHEET]/[ASSUMED] provenance.
#
# GENERIC_600_600: representative 600:600 line transformer. NickelIron (line/mic
#   cores). Rated ~+20 dBu @20Hz [ASSUMED, line-transformer class]. Derived knee
#   a≈656 A/m; h_peak ≈278 at +4 dBu (linear), ≈1750 at +20 dBu (JA).
.TRANSFORMER GENERIC_600_600 LP=1 K=0.995 RP=50 RS=50 LLP=5m LLS=5m LM=995m RC=200k CP=50p N1=1200 N2=1200 AE=5e-4 LE=0.06 MS=6e5
# GENERIC_10K_10K: representative 10k:10k bridging/interstage. NickelIron. Rated
#   ~+20 dBu @20Hz [ASSUMED]. Derived knee a≈149; h_peak ≈42 (+4 dBu, linear),
#   ≈263 (+20 dBu, JA).
.TRANSFORMER GENERIC_10K_10K LP=10 K=0.995 RP=500 RS=500 LLP=50m LLS=50m LM=9.95 RC=1MEG CP=75p N1=2400 N2=2400 AE=3e-4 LE=0.08 MS=6e5
# JT11P1: Jensen JT-11P-1, 1:1 line input. NickelIron (Jensen uses 80% Ni-Fe
#   cores). Rated +20 dBu @20Hz [DATASHEET, jensen-transformers.com]. Derived
#   knee a≈332; h_peak ≈163 (+4 dBu, linear), ≈1027 (+20 dBu, JA).
.TRANSFORMER JT11P1 LP=2 K=0.99 RP=75 RS=75 LLP=20m LLS=20m LM=1.98 RC=500k CP=200p N1=1400 N2=1400 AE=3.5e-4 LE=0.06 MS=6e5
# JT10KB-D: Jensen JT-10KB-D, 4:1 stepdown line input. NickelIron. Rated
#   +21 dBu @20Hz [DATASHEET, jensen-transformers.com]. Derived knee a≈149;
#   h_peak ≈42 (+4 dBu, linear), ≈295 (+21 dBu, JA).
.TRANSFORMER JT10KB-D LP=10 K=0.995 RP=600 RS=150 LLP=50m LLS=12.5m LM=9.95 RC=1MEG CP=100p N1=2400 N2=600 AE=3e-4 LE=0.08 MS=6e5
# A262A2E: large interstage transformer (Lm≈30H). NickelIron. Rated ~+24 dBu
#   @20Hz [ASSUMED, no datasheet found for this part]. Derived knee a≈85;
#   h_peak ≈14 (+4 dBu, linear), ≈138 (+24 dBu, JA).
.TRANSFORMER A262A2E LP=30 K=0.998 RP=1200 RS=300 LLP=60m LLS=15m LM=29.94 RC=2MEG CP=120p N1=3000 N2=1500 AE=3e-4 LE=0.10 MS=6e5

# Gapped single-ended output-transformer demo from the Phase-2 J-A prototype.
# The magnetic parameters are behavioral test data, not a verified product fit.
# Geometry made SELF-CONSISTENT (2026-06-16): the old AE=2e-4 was geometrically
# inconsistent with LM=9.97 H (forced a diamagnetic χ<0), which is why the
# library carried an explicit A=1100 as a workaround. AE=4.364e-3 makes the
# DERIVED knee (`from_small_signal`, SiliconSteel, LM=9.97, N1=2000, LE=0.10,
# GAP=1e-3) equal the validated a≈1100 — so this part now derives `a` through
# the SAME path as the whole library, no explicit-`a` special case. ALPHA/JA_K/
# JA_C remain as hysteresis-SHAPE overrides (ALPHA matches the SiliconSteel
# default, so the Lm-pinned tangent is unaffected). [ASSUMED behavioral test fit]
.TRANSFORMER OT-DEMO-SE LP=10 K=0.997 RP=270 RS=0.5 LLP=30m LLS=1.2u LM=9.97 CP=200p N1=2000 N2=76.923076923 AE=4.364e-3 LE=0.10 GAP=1e-3 IDC=45m MS=1.6e6 ALPHA=1.6e-3 JA_K=400 JA_C=0.2
